    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the single `POST /api/owners` create path. Before persisting a new owner, it now rejects with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, reusing the existing case-insensitive `countOwnersInCity` helper:\n\n```java\nif (countOwnersInCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity()) >= 50) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\nThe test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`, which fills a city to 50 and expects the 51st to be rejected).",
